/* en-zh deck "Compliments", writer of docs/briefs/compliments.md. One card per line: target | pron | meaning | note. pron generated by tools/target/zh/respell.js (with lexicon-add-C.txt), never typed. */
module.exports = {
  "Compliments": `
真香！ | Zhēn xiāng! | It smells amazing! | Said about food as it arrives. Online, 真香 is also a joke about eating your words.
你做的菜真好吃！ | Nǐ zuò de cài zhēn hǎochī! | Your cooking is delicious! | Lit. "the dishes you make are really tasty". To an older host: 您做的菜真好吃！
做得很好！ | Zuò de hěn hǎo! | Well done! / Good job! | Praise for work or homework. Sounds like a teacher or boss; between friends 你真棒 is warmer.
你真厉害！ | Nǐ zhēn lìhai! | You're really good at this! | The everyday "wow, impressive!" for any skill. Fine to friends, colleagues, anyone your age.
好主意！ | Hǎo zhǔyi! | That's a great idea! | Short and casual. A full sentence: 这个主意真好。
你人真好。 | Nǐ rén zhēn hǎo. | You're so kind. | Lit. "you, as a person, are really good". Often said right after someone helps you.
你真幽默！ | Nǐ zhēn yōumò! | You're really funny! | 幽默 is "witty, has a sense of humor", a real compliment. Not 你真好笑, which can mean "you're ridiculous".
你真努力！ | Nǐ zhēn nǔlì! | You work so hard! | Praise for effort, much valued in China. Fine to friends, classmates and colleagues.
你家真漂亮！ | Nǐ jiā zhēn piàoliang! | Your home is beautiful! | A natural thing to say as a guest. 家 is both "home" and "family"; here it is the home.
你穿这件真好看！ | Nǐ chuān zhè jiàn zhēn hǎokàn! | You look great in that! | Lit. "you wear this one, really good-looking". 件 is for tops, coats, dresses; for trousers say 这条.
你中文说得真好！ | Nǐ Zhōngwén shuō de zhēn hǎo! | Your Chinese is really good! | You will hear this a lot, often after you say just 你好. Answer modestly (see 哪里哪里 and 还差得远呢).
你的发音很标准。 | Nǐ de fāyīn hěn biāozhǔn. | Your pronunciation is really good. | Lit. "your pronunciation is very standard". 标准 is the usual praise for accent.
哪里哪里。 | Nǎlǐ nǎlǐ. | Oh, not at all. (modest reply) | Lit. "where? where?": the classic modest way to brush off praise. Older people and formal settings expect it; young people often just say 谢谢.
过奖了。 | Guòjiǎng le. | You flatter me. | A polite, slightly formal modest reply: "you praise me too much". Good with older people or at work.
还差得远呢。 | Hái chà de yuǎn ne. | I still have a long way to go. | The usual reply when someone praises your Chinese. Accepting praise outright can sound boastful; 谢谢 alone is also fine today.
`,
};
